<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Bank to offer Visa cards end-1996.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank to offer Visa cards end-1996.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG, Germany's biggest commercial bank, will start issuing Visa credit cards in Germany later this year, Visa said on Friday.</p>
<p>Deutsche has agreed to join a group of German banks to become a &quot;dual issuer&quot; -- meaning it will offer both Eurocards and Visa cards.</p>
<p>Visa said in a statement that Deutsche would offer customers Visa Classic and Visa Gold cards.</p>
<p>Visa is one of the world's largest consumer credit card issuers with about 20,000 member banks and more than 500 million cards in circulation worldwide.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
